From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+alilinux@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:40:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mips: gate TLB/page-table/vdso machinery out of nommu
 build: P3

Build gating (docs/nommu_mipsel_implementation.md, patch P3):

arch/mips/mm/Makefile:
- fault.o gup.o mmap.o tlbex.o tlbex-fault.o tlb-funcs.o and
  pgtable-{32,64}.o only under CONFIG_MMU (conditional vars -- names
  must not match the .o basenames or Kbuild treats them as composite
  parts and builds nothing).
- ioremap.o MMU-only; new ioremap-nommu.c provides __ioremap/__iounmap
  over the fixed kseg1 window (low 512MB uncached), rejecting anything
  else -- there are no page tables to remap into.
- tlb-r4k.o split out of the cache lines (c-r4k.o cex-gen.o must stay:
  the C3503D needs R4K cache maintenance) via mmu-tlb-y.
- uasm stays unconditional: arch/mips/mm/page.c uses it to build
  clear_page/copy_page.

arch/mips/kernel: vdso.o MMU-only; GENERIC_TIME_VSYSCALL is selected only
with MMU, so timekeeping needs no update_vsyscall() hooks.
arch/mips/Kbuild: vdso/ MMU-only.  Kconfig: CPU_GENERIC_DUMP_TLB
depends on MMU (no TLB to dump).

Source ifdefs:
- traps.c: handle_tlb* vector installs (1..3), tlb_do_page_fault_0
  (RIXI ex. 19/20), tlb_init()/TLBMISS_HANDLER_SETUP(),
  TLBMISS_HANDLER_RESTORE() in the PM notifier, ASID_FIRST_VERSION and
  the dump_tlb block in do_mcheck.
- mm/init.c: pagetable_init()/kmap_init() in paging_init (zones only
  for nommu), the wired-TLB kmap card (__kmap_pgprot and friends)
  replaced by kseg0 stubs (cpu_has_dc_aliases == 0 makes them dead),
  fixrange_init users gone, swapper_pg_dir/invalid_*_table/pgd_current
  MMU-only, plus nommu definitions of shm_align_mask,
  show_unhandled_signals and __virt_addr_valid (moved out of mmap.c/
  fault.c).
- mm/cache.c: __update_cache()/setup_protection_map() MMU-only.
- mm/c-r4k.c: has_valid_asid and the page-table-walking flush_cache_
  {mm,range,page} implementations MMU-only, with no-op nommu versions
  so the cache_ops wiring still links.
- signal.c: nommu sigreturn trampolines in kernel text (userland runs
  in kernel mode, no vdso to borrow): li v0,__NR{,_rt}_sigreturn;
  syscall -- verified in disassembly (4119/4193).  abi->vdso
  initializers gated in signal.c/signal32.c/signal_n32.c.
- asm/elf.h: ARCH_DLINFO (AT_SYSINFO_EHDR) and
  ARCH_HAS_SETUP_ADDITIONAL_PAGES MMU-only; binfmt_elf.c tolerates an
  absent ARCH_DLINFO (#ifdef).

Nommu vmlinux links; System.map contains zero TLB/vdso symbols.
Regression (malta, MMU=y): full vmlinux builds, TLB/vdso symbols
back.  Only warnings left are pre-existing GCC14 -fcommon COMMON-symbol
modpost noise and kernel/sched/core.c -Waddress (both also on the
pristine tree).
